- **`ExcludeSelf bool`** (`effects.go:235`) — used together with a broad filter for "each OTHER creature" (checked at `effects.go:1620-1622`: `if e.ExcludeSelf && e.SourceID == card.ID { return false }`).
- **"Each creature you control" / "each creature"**: no `.Each`-style construct — expressed by leaving `AffectsSpecific` empty and setting `AffectsFilter` ("creature"/"permanent"/"land"/"artifact_creature"/etc., `effects.go:232`, matched at `1625-1659`) plus `AffectsController` ("you"/"opponent"/"any", `effects.go:234`, matched at `1767-1784`). Enchant/"affects enchanted" permanent is `AffectsEnchanted bool` (`effects.go:237`, matched `1611-1617`).
- Many further narrowing predicates compose onto the same filter (subtype, exclude-subtype, token/nontoken, counter-type presence, color/exclude-color, colorless, legendary, attacking, blocking, modified, tapped/untapped, multicolored, commander, keyword, and an arbitrary `AffectsPredicateFn func(card *Card) bool` escape hatch at `effects.go:302-314`), all ANDed together in `effectAffectsCard`.

For a `switch_pt` effect targeting one creature "until end of turn," the natural fit is `AffectsSpecific: <target card ID>` + `UntilEOT: true`, mirroring how existing single-target EOT pump effects (e.g. `PowerMod`/`ToughnessMod` with `AffectsSpecific`) are already registered elsewhere in `ability_effects.go`.

